// Per-connection rate limit (P3 flow state): count data segments on each
// connection and ban the source once it floods.
//
// `flow.count` reads-then-increments a counter living in the per-flow map — the
// only state the XDP verifier lets evolve across packets, because it is
// laundered through a map lookup each time rather than kept on the stack. `ban`
// adds the source IP to a blocklist map for a TTL, so later packets are dropped
// before this program even runs.
reassemble 8080;
filter {
  if (len == 0) return pass;            // pure ACKs don't count
  if (flow.count >= 100) {
    log(1);                             // emit an event for userspace
    return ban("flood", 600);          // ban the source for 600 seconds
  }
  return pass;
}
